Q: Does Azure have an out-of-box way of distributed locking with a key? A: <p>Since you mentioned ActivityTrigger so i am assuming that you are using the DurableFunction.</p>
<p>I guess you can use Durable entities.</p>
<pre><code> [Function(nameof(LockEntity))]
    public static Task RunEntityAsync([EntityTrigger] TaskEntityDispatcher dispatcher) =&gt;
        dispatcher.DispatchAsync(_ =&gt; default);
</code></pre>

Q: Programmatically check the version name of TranslatePress plugin for WordPress A: <p>𝟭. Use WordPress native is_plugin_active()</p>
<p>Instead of relying on internal class properties, check for the active plugin slug directly:</p>
<pre><code>function tp_get_license_tier(): string {
    if ( ! function_exists( 'is_plugin_active' ) ) {
        require_once ABSPATH . 'wp-admin/includes/plugin.php';
    }

    $tiers = [
        'developer' =&gt; 'translatepress-developer/index.php',
        'business'  =&gt; 'translatepress-business/index.php',
        'personal'  =&gt; 'translatepress-personal/index.php',
    ];

    foreach ( $tiers as $tier =&gt; $path ) {
        if ( is_plugin_active( $path ) ) {
            return $tier;
        }
    }

    return 'free';
}
</code></pre>
<p>✅ Uses WordPress core API ✅ Won't break if TranslatePress refactors internals ✅ Returns a meaningful value</p>
<p>━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p>
<p>𝟮. Get the actual version number with get_plugin_data()</p>
<pre><code>function tp_get_version(): string {
    if ( ! function_exists( 'get_plugin_data' ) ) {
        require_once ABSPATH . 'wp-admin/includes/plugin.php';
    }

    $file = WP_PLUGIN_DIR . '/translatepress-multilingual/index.php';

    if ( ! file_exists( $file ) ) {
        return '0.0.0';
    }

    $data = get_plugin_data( $file, false, false );
    return $data['Version'] ?? '0.0.0';
}
</code></pre>
<p>This reads version directly from the plugin file headers the most reliable source.</p>
<p>━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p>
<p>𝟯. Combine both for the full picture</p>
<pre><code>function tp_get_full_info(): array {
    if ( ! function_exists( 'get_plugin_data' ) ) {
        require_once ABSPATH . 'wp-admin/includes/plugin.php';
    }

    $base = WP_PLUGIN_DIR . '/translatepress-multilingual/index.php';

    if ( ! file_exists( $base ) ) {
        return [ 'installed' =&gt; false, 'tier' =&gt; 'none', 'version' =&gt; '0.0.0' ];
    }

    $data = get_plugin_data( $base, false, false );
    $tier = 'free';

    foreach ( [ 'developer', 'business', 'personal' ] as $t ) {
        if ( is_plugin_active( &quot;translatepress-{$t}/index.php&quot; ) ) {
            $tier = $t;
            break;
        }
    }

    return [
        'installed' =&gt; true,
        'tier'      =&gt; $tier,
        'version'   =&gt; $data['Version'] ?? '0.0.0',
    ];
}
</code></pre>
